You are an expert assistant in configuring network devices. Based on the user's request and the retrieved content from the router configuration manual below, generate appropriate CLI configuration commands.

---

User Request:  
Hey, I'm working on a Nokia 7750 SR where I need to tweak BGP so it can share up to 8 different next-hop options for the same plain IPv4 destination (no MPLS labels involved) with a neighbor. Also, I want the router to ask peers nicely to send multiple route choices back for each prefix—like handling a traffic jam by suggesting alternate roads. Any config snippets or hidden knobs to make this happen without breaking route reflection?

Retrieved Reference Content (from the configuration manual):  
{
    "PageTitle": "use-bgp-routes",
    "FuncDef": "This command specifies whether to use BGP routes to recursively resolve the BGP next-hop of unlabeled IPv4 and unlabeled IPv6 routes. Up to four levels of recursion are supported.",
    "CLIs": [
        "use-bgp-routes",
        "no use-bgp-routes"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp>next-hop-res"
    ],
    "ParaDef": null,
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no use-bgp-routes"
}
{
    "PageTitle": "backup-path",
    "FuncDef": "This command enables the computation and use of a backup path for IPv4 and/or IPv6 BGP-learned prefixes belonging to the base router. Multiple paths must be received for a prefix in order to take advantage of this feature. When a prefix has a backup path and its primary paths fail, the affected traffic is rapidly diverted to the backup path without waiting for control plane re-convergence to occur. When many prefixes share the same primary paths, and in some cases also the same backup path, the time to failover traffic to the backup path is independent of the number of prefixes.",
    "CLIs": [
        "backup-path [ ipv4 ] [ ipv6 ] [ label-ipv4 ] [ label-ipv6 ]",
        "no backup-path [ ipv4 ] [ ipv6 ] [ label-ipv4 ] [ label-ipv6 ]"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp"
    ],
    "ParaDef": [
        {
            "Parameters": "ipv4",
            "Info": "Enables BGP fast reroute for unlabeled unicast IPv4 routes."
        },
        {
            "Parameters": "ipv6",
            "Info": "Enables BGP fast reroute for unlabeled unicast IPv6 routes."
        },
        {
            "Parameters": "label-ipv4",
            "Info": "Enables BGP fast reroute for labeled-unicast IPv4 routes."
        },
        {
            "Parameters": "label-ipv6",
            "Info": "Enables BGP fast reroute for labeled-unicast IPv6 routes."
        }
    ],
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no backup-path"
}
{
    "PageTitle": "next-hop-self",
    "FuncDef": "This command configures BGP to advertise routes to members of a group or to a specific neighbor using a local address of the BGP instance as the BGP next-hop address. Note thatnext-hop-selfis set without exception, regardless of the route source (EBGP or IBGP) or its family. When used with VPN-IPv4 and VPN-IPv6 routes theenable-rr-vpn-forwardingcommand should also be configured.",
    "CLIs": [
        "next-hop-self",
        "no next-hop-self"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
