To ensure BGP consistently weighs MED numbers when selecting routes from different neighboring ASes, use the following configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp best-path-selection
    deterministic-med
    always-compare-med zero
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enables deterministic MED comparison by grouping paths from the same neighbor AS before MED evaluation
2. Forces MED comparison across paths from different ASes
3. Treats routes without a MED attribute as having a value of 0 during comparisons

The combination ensures MED is always evaluated as the tie-breaker between paths from different ASes, maintaining consistent path selection.
