## Proposed answer:
To automatically add the link-bandwidth extended community to IPv4 routes received from directly connected external BGP neighbors, use the following configuration:

```cli
configure router
    bgp
        group "EBGP_GROUP"
            link-bandwidth
                add-to-received-ebgp ipv4
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- Apply this under your BGP group configuration for external neighbors (replace `EBGP_GROUP` with your actual group name).  
- The `link-bandwidth` command enters the context for bandwidth-related attributes.  
- `add-to-received-ebgp ipv4` automatically appends the link-bandwidth community to IPv4 routes received from directly connected eBGP peers.  

**Note:** Ensure the neighbors are directly connected (single-hop) for this to take effect.
