To set up a placeholder routing instance for MPLS-based VPN routes and ensure they resolve BGP next-hops, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    enable-rr-vpn-forwarding
    next-hop-resolution
        use-bgp-routes
    exit
exit
```

### Explanation:
- **`enable-rr-vpn-forwarding`**: Imports all received VPN-IP routes (regardless of route target) into a dummy VRF. This allows BGP next-hops to be resolved using these routes.
- **`use-bgp-routes`**: Enables BGP to recursively resolve next-hops for unlabeled IPv4/IPv6 routes using BGP routes (up to 4 levels of recursion). This ensures the placeholder routes influence next-hop decisions for other traffic.
