User Request:  
Hey, I’m working on a Nokia 7750 SR where I need to set up BGP to share multiple IPv6 routes with labels for the same destination—like up to 8 options per network block. How do I tweak the config so it both sends that many and can handle getting multiple routes back from neighbors without tripping any defaults? Running into issues where it only picks one path even though the peer supports more.

