To configure BGP to prioritize routes with the lowest total internal path cost (IGP metric), enable the AIGP attribute on relevant BGP peers. This ensures BGP path selection uses the cumulative IGP metric:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group "internal-peers"
        aigp
    exit
exit
```

**Key points:**  
- AIGP propagates end-to-end IGP metrics across BGP paths, even between ASes.  
- Paths with lower AIGP values are preferred during BGP best-path selection.  
- Apply this to all iBGP peers in the path (e.g., route reflectors, edge routers).  

For specific neighbors, configure under their individual settings:
```cli
