To prevent routes from being reflected back to the same cluster members in a BGP route reflection setup on Nokia 7750 SR, enable the `split-horizon` feature for the specific group containing the route reflector clients. This ensures routes learned from a peer in the group are not advertised back to that same peer.

```cli
/configure router bgp group "RR_CLUSTER_GROUP" 
    split-horizon
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- Replace `"RR_CLUSTER_GROUP"` with your actual BGP group name configured for route reflection clients.
- The `split-horizon` command explicitly blocks routes received from a peer from being reflected back to that peer within the same group, resolving the "boomerang" effect. By default, this feature is disabled (`no split-horizon`), so enabling it is necessary to enforce this behavior.
