To configure your BGP neighbor clusters to handle unexpected error messages without dropping sessions during polite reboots, use the following commands:

```
configure router bgp group "your-group-name"
    graceful-restart
        enable-notification
    exit
exit
```

**Key details:**
- Replace `"your-group-name"` with your actual BGP group name
- `enable-notification` allows sessions to restart gracefully when NOTIFICATION messages are sent
- Both peers must support this capability for graceful session restart to work
- This configuration is applied at the BGP group level for all neighbors in the cluster

For comprehensive error handling, consider also enabling:
```
configure router bgp group "your-group-name"
    error-handling
        update-fault-tolerance
    exit
exit
```
This handles UPDATE message errors non-disruptively without session resets.
