2. **`extended-nh-encoding vpn-ipv4`**: Advertises the capability to accept VPN-IPv4 routes carrying IPv6 next-hops during the BGP session establishment. This explicitly signals to the peer that your router can process these routes.  

This configuration ensures your router includes the required capability in the BGP OPEN message, informing the neighbor it can handle IPv6 next-hops for VPN-IPv4 routes.
