## User question:
Hey, on a Nokia box running BGP for labeled IPv6, how can I tweak the path decision to make it consider external and internal neighbor routes the same? I have routes from both external and internal peers, but the box is preferring the external ones even though the internal paths have better metrics.
---
## Proposed answer:
To adjust the BGP path selection for labeled IPv6 routes to treat external and internal peers equally, configure the BGP best path selection to ignore the router ID comparison for internal routes. Use the following commands:

```cli
configure router bgp best-path-selection
ignore-router-id include-internal mvpn-ipv6
exit
```

This configuration ensures the BGP best-path algorithm does not prefer external paths over internal paths solely based on the external peer type, allowing metrics to determine the best path.
