To make BGP sessions more resilient to brief physical link flaps on your Nokia 7750 SR, use the following configuration commands. These adjustments ensure BGP relies on the hold timer for session stability instead of reacting immediately to transient link issues:

```cli
configure router bgp
    disable-fast-external-failover
    no enable-peer-tracking
exit
```

### Explanation:
1. **`disable-fast-external-failover`**  
   Prevents BGP from instantly tearing down sessions when a physical link fluctuates. Instead, BGP will wait for the hold timer to expire before declaring the peer down.

2. **`no enable-peer-tracking`**  
   Stops BGP from immediately dropping sessions if the underlying route to the peer is briefly removed. This works with `disable-fast-external-failover` to enforce hold-timer-based failure detection.

### Key Behavior:
- BGP will now wait for the **hold timer duration** (default 90 seconds) to detect peer failures.  
- Sessions stay up during sub-second link "blips" (e.g., fiber flaps), as long as the interruption is shorter than the hold timer.  
- Adjust the global `hold-time` (e.g., `hold-time 120`) if you need a longer failure detection window.
