## User question:
On a Nokia 7750 SR, when I have multiple identical path options from BGP neighbors in the default routing instance, how do I stop the routing process from caring about how "far" the next-hop appears to be in the IGP’s eyes during best-path selection? I’m seeing routes flip unpredictably because of this.
