## Proposed answer:
To adjust your BGP settings for recognizing and processing path capacity metrics from external peers, configure the following commands:

```
configure router bgp group <external-group-name> 
   aigp
```

Replace `<external-group-name>` with the appropriate BGP group name for your external neighbors. This command enables processing of the Accumulated IGP (AIGP) metric attribute, which handles path capacity information shared by peers.

For neighbor-specific configuration:
```
configure router bgp group <external-group-name> neighbor <peer-ip>
   aigp
```
Replace `<peer-ip>` with the specific neighbor's IP address. This setting allows path selection based on end-to-end IGP metrics across AS boundaries.
