To configure BGP to use your pre-defined static routes for next-hop resolution on tagged customer traffic and private network routes, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
/configure router policy-options
begin
prefix-list "CUSTOM_PATHS"
    prefix 10.1.1.0/24 exact
    prefix 10.2.2.0/24 exact
exit
policy-statement "STATIC_NH_POLICY"
    entry 10
        from
            prefix-list "CUSTOM_PATHS"
        exit
        action accept
        exit
    exit
    default-action reject
exit
commit
/configure router bgp next-hop-res
    policy "STATIC_NH_POLICY"
exit
/configure router bgp next-hop-resolution labeled-routes
    allow-static
exit
```

### Key details:
1. **`prefix-list "CUSTOM_PATHS"`**: Replace `10.1.1.0/24` and `10.2.2.0/24` with your specific pre-defined static route prefixes
2. **`policy-statement "STATIC_NH_POLICY"`**: Explicitly permits your static routes for BGP next-hop resolution while rejecting all others
3. **`next-hop-res policy`**: Forces BGP to use only your approved static routes for unlabeled IPv4/IPv6 next-hop resolution
4. **`labeled-routes allow-static`**: Enables static route usage for resolving next-hops of labeled routes (e.g., VPN traffic)

