To apply the "INTERNAL-BGP" policy for outbound BGP updates to peers, use the following CLI commands. Replace `<group-name>` and `<ip-address>` with your specific BGP group or neighbor details:  

```  
configure router bgp group <group-name>  
    export "INTERNAL-BGP"  
exit  

configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>  
    export "INTERNAL-BGP"  
exit  
```  

**Key Notes**:  
- Apply `export "INTERNAL-BGP"` at either the **BGP group level** (affects all peers in the group) or **per neighbor** (specific peer).  
- Ensure the policy "INTERNAL-BGP" is already defined in `config>router>policy-options` with prefix-filtering rules.  
- This policy will filter prefixes advertised to the specified peers.  

**Example for a neighbor in group "EBGP_PEERS"**:  
```  
configure router bgp group "EBGP_PEERS" neighbor 192.0.2.1  
    export "INTERNAL-BGP"  
```
