Based on your request to display a custom message to BGP monitoring (BMP) clients upon connection, use the following CLI configuration. This leverages the `contact` parameter under the BMP station configuration to send the specified text during session initialization:

```cli
configure router bgp
    monitor
        station "STATION_NAME"
            contact "If issues, ping support@example.com or ring +1-555-1234567"
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Key details:**  
- Replace `"STATION_NAME"` with the actual name of your BMP monitoring station.  
- The `contact` command injects your custom message into the BMP initiation message sent immediately after the session handshake.  
- The text will be visible in the BMP client's logs or interface upon successful connection.  

