## User question:
Hey, on a Nokia 7750 SR, if I adjust the rules for how VPN routes are handled, how do I stop the router from dumping the BGP routes it already received from neighbors? I want it to keep all the multi-family BGP paths in its incoming table without making peers resend everything after policy tweaks.
---
## Proposed answer:
To prevent the router from discarding BGP routes after VPN policy adjustments and retain all multi-family BGP paths without requiring peers to resend, use the following configuration:

```bash
configure router bgp
    mp-bgp-keep
exit
```

This command ensures RIB-IN retains all MP-BGP routes during policy changes and stops route refresh messages from being triggered.
