To set up RSVP-based paths for optimal BGP route selection, configure BGP to resolve next hops using RSVP tunnels with the lowest metric:

```
configure router
    bgp
        next-hop-resolution
            shortcut-tunn
                family ipv4
                    resolution-filter rsvp
                exit
            exit
            labeled-routes
                transport-tunnel
                    family ipv4
                        resolution-filter rsvp
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

**Key notes:**
- BGP automatically selects the RSVP tunnel with the lowest metric to the next hop.
- When multiple RSVP tunnels have identical metrics, BGP chooses the tunnel with the lowest tunnel ID.
- This configuration applies to both unlabeled (`shortcut-tunn`) and labeled (`labeled-routes`) IPv4 routes. Repeat for `ipv6` if needed.
