To handle wonky BGP UPDATE messages without tearing down sessions, enable `update-fault-tolerance` under the BGP neighbor's error handling configuration. This forces the router to treat malformed NLRI updates as withdrawals instead of resetting the session:

```cli
configure router bgp
    neighbor <neighbor-ip>
        error-handling
            update-fault-tolerance
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<neighbor-ip>` with the problematic neighbor's IP. This applies specifically to NLRI errors that don't involve message length corruption. For broader application, use `group` or global BGP contexts instead of `neighbor`.
