To configure BGP on your Nokia 7750 SR to set the MED (metric) field using OSPF/IS-IS internal path costs, create a route policy that sets the MED to the IGP metric and apply it as an export policy to your BGP group or neighbor. This ensures neighboring ASes receive MED values reflecting your actual path costs:

```cli
/configure router policy-options
begin
policy-statement "SET_MED"
    entry 10
        from protocol [ospf isis]
        action accept
            set metric (igp-metric)
        exit
    exit
    entry 20
        action accept
    exit
exit
commit
exit

/configure router bgp
group "eBGP_Group"  # Replace with your BGP group/neighbor name
    export "SET_MED"
exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- The policy `SET_MED` matches routes learned via OSPF/IS-IS and sets the MED (`metric`) to the IGP cost of the path (`(igp-metric)`).
- Entry 20 ensures other routes (e.g., static, direct) are advertised without MED modification.
- Applying this policy as an `export` to your BGP group propagates the MED to eBGP peers.

**Verification:**  
After configuration, check advertised routes to confirm MED values:
```cli
show router bgp neighbor <ip-address> advertised-routes
```
