To address the issue of BGP being chatty with route changes for unstable prefixes, enabling BGP route damping is the appropriate solution. Route damping suppresses flapping routes and controls the advertisement timing for unstable prefixes. Here are the CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    damping
```

**Note**: The `damping` command must be coupled with a **route policy** that defines damping parameters (half-life, reuse threshold, suppress threshold, and max suppress time). For a 60-second minimum wait, configure the damping profile in the route policy with a half-life of 60 seconds and a reuse threshold of 500 (ensuring at least one half-life must pass before re-advertising the prefix). Example policy snippet:

```cli
configure router policy-options
    begin
    policy-statement "DAMPING_PROFILE"
        entry 10
            damping
                half-life 60
                reuse 500
                suppress 2000
                max-suppress 240
            exit
        exit
    commit
exit
```

